# This project uses the public npm registry only.
#
# Local development machines may configure a corporate npm proxy as the default
# registry in ~/.npmrc (e.g. an internal Artifactory). If that proxy is slow or
# unreachable, Vaadin's dev-mode `npm install` (TaskRunNpmInstall) hangs for
# minutes and then fails with "Npm install has exited with non zero status",
# and the lockfile gets re-resolved against corporate URLs — which
# NpmLockfileRegistryTest then rejects. A project-level .npmrc overrides
# ~/.npmrc for every npm invocation inside this directory (including the
# Vaadin plugin's own node/npm toolchain), keeping dev mode and CI on the
# public registry.
registry=https://registry.npmjs.org/
